**1. A system for detecting an allergen in a food sample, the system comprising:**

a homogenization assembly configured to homogenize the food sample with a liquid to produce a sample homogenate;

a mixing chamber fluidly coupled to the homogenization assembly and configured to combine at least a portion of the sample homogenate with a reagent that selectively interacts with the allergen to produce a detectable response;

a detection substrate positioned to receive at least a portion of the combined sample homogenate and reagent, the detection substrate comprising a test region configured to indicate the detectable response;

an optical sensor arranged to acquire optical measurement data from the test region; and

a controller operatively coupled to the optical sensor and configured to determine, based on the optical measurement data, whether the allergen is present in the food sample.

**2. A method for detecting an allergen in a food sample, the method comprising:**

homogenizing the food sample with a liquid to produce a sample homogenate;

mixing at least a portion of the sample homogenate with a reagent that selectively interacts with the allergen to produce a detectable response;

delivering at least a portion of the mixed sample homogenate and reagent to a detection substrate comprising a test region;

acquiring, with an optical sensor, optical measurement data from the test region; and

determining, based on the optical measurement data, whether the allergen is present in the food sample.

1. **A device for detecting an allergen in a consumable sample, the device comprising:**

a first chamber configured to receive the consumable sample;

a second chamber in fluid communication with the first chamber and comprising an outlet port;

a process reagent disposed within at least one of the first chamber or the second chamber and configured to interact with the consumable sample to produce a processed sample;

an analysis chamber in fluid communication with the outlet port and configured to receive the processed sample;

a detection substrate disposed within the analysis chamber and comprising a binding agent configured to selectively bind the allergen and generate an optically detectable signal in response to binding of the allergen; and

an optical sensor positioned to detect the optically detectable signal from the detection substrate,

wherein the device is configured to determine a presence or an amount of the allergen in the consumable sample based on an output of the optical sensor.
